  "notes": [
    "Read by bin/copilot-model-refresh.py (copilot-s menu p). It is NOT a routing config: shipped routing defaults stay in config/agent-routing.yaml and agents/*.agent.md and are never changed by a refresh.",
    "Every field below is transcribed from the official GitHub docs pages listed in 'sources' on reviewed_on. They are categorical labels only (official pricing Category, official model-comparison Task area, official extended-capability and per-client support). They are NOT quality scores or benchmarks, and nothing here is inferred from price or release date.",
    "Live prices are never read from this file: they are fetched at refresh time from the official pricing page. A model whose live official Category differs from the one recorded here is treated as needing re-review and is never proposed.",
    "Route policy (unless a route override is given): a replacement must have the same official Task area as the route's shipped baseline model, an official Category at least as high, official configurable-reasoning support, official 1M-context support when the route uses long_context, be listed as included for Copilot CLI, be in the user's verified availability list, and have the route's specific reasoning level verified for that model. This mapping is toolkit policy; the shipped baselines remain the recommendation, not an independent quality measure.",
    "Specific reasoning levels: the official docs only document configurable reasoning as a yes/no capability and say the levels vary per model (Copilot CLI shows them only in its interactive /model picker). No model below therefore has 'reasoning_levels'; that optional field may be added only with a source that documents the levels for that model. Until then a replacement needs the user's dated verified_capabilities record in user-config.json — an unknown level always fails closed.",
    "This catalog is the documented FALLBACK, not an allowlist: on each refresh the tool also fetches the official supported-models and model-comparison pages and, per model and field, uses that fresh live evidence when it can be parsed and attributed (a live value that differs from this file is shown as a change; one that contradicts a LOCAL overlay entry fails closed). A model absent from this file (for example a new model in the official pricing) is assessed from the live pages when they document its task area, Category, capabilities and Copilot CLI support; otherwise it is listed as unassessed and never assigned. To vet a model the live pages do not cover, add a dated entry (with sources) to the local catalog overlay in <COPILOT_HOME>/model-refresh/user-config.json, or update this file and its reviewed_on/expires_on dates."
  ],
